<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PathAssistant xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        The BROKER-LISTED disposition path, for the On_Market record type.
        REBUILT 2026-08-19 to the redesigned ELEVEN steps: Disposition Readiness, BOV Outreach,
        Broker Selection, NDA, Release Materials, Active Listing, Offer Selection, LOI, PSA,
        Closing, Sale Closes.

        =====================================================================================
        WHAT CHANGED AND WHY, STEP BY STEP - so nobody has to diff this against git to find out.
        =====================================================================================
        REMOVED: the Call for Offers step and the Completed step. Call for Offers is a retired
        stage value; Completed was renamed by replacement to Sale Closes.
        ADDED: Broker Selection, Release Materials, Offer Selection, Sale Closes.
        🔴 NDA IS NOW ON THIS PATH. The doctrine that "NDA and Disposition Offer are off-market
        stage values ONLY", which stood in both record-type files, in
        All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression and in lwc/dispositionSidebar.js, is DEAD. An
        on-market deal collects NDAs from interested parties before materials are released, and
        All_NDAs_Signed_Before_Progression dropped its record-type term in the same change - so
        the release gate now fires on THIS path too.

        ⚠ TWO ORPHAN STEPS WILL RENDER AFTER Sale Closes UNTIL THE PICKLIST CLEANUP WAVE RUNS.
        Call for Offers and Completed still exist as values and are still listed on the
        On_Market record type (a record type cannot reference a deleted value, and a metadata
        deploy cannot delete one - Setup can). They have NO step here, so they render with no
        guidance. That is deliberate: stale guidance on a stage nothing should reach is worse
        than none. Zero records sit on either value.

        WHAT EACH STEP'S EXIT IS OWNED BY - this is the single most useful thing on this page,
        because the Advance button is NOT available at every step:
            Disposition Readiness -> BOV Outreach     Sale Decision approval (auto-advance)
            BOV Outreach -> Broker Selection          Broker Finalize approval on the BOV
            Broker Selection -> NDA                   MANUAL: Advance to NDA
            NDA -> Release Materials                  MANUAL: Advance to Release Materials
            Release Materials -> Active Listing       MANUAL: Advance to Active Listing
            Active Listing -> Offer Selection         Select Offer (service DML)
            Offer Selection -> LOI                    Offer Selection approval on the offer
            LOI -> PSA                                MANUAL: Advance to PSA
            PSA -> Closing                            ContractExecutionService, on PSA execution
            Closing -> Sale Closes                    Closing approval (auto-advance)
        RecordStageAdvanceService's CONFIG_BY_TYPE holds ONLY the four manual hops, so the
        Advance button structurally cannot skip an approval-owned or machine-owned one.

        Listing_Date__c WAS ADDED to the Active Listing step's fieldNames. Its info text has
        told the user since 2026-08-10 that the marketing clock does not start until that date is
        set, while offering no field to set it from - the same
        describes-a-workflow-nobody-can-perform defect that Disposition_Record_Page's ndasList
        note records. Both permission sets already carry the field (Edit has it editable).

        THE ACTIVE LISTING TEXT WAS REWRITTEN 2026-08-21 AND THE RULE THAT FROZE IT IS RETRACTED.
        RETRACTED - was: "THE ACTIVE LISTING TEXT IS COPIED BYTE-IDENTICAL FROM THE PREVIOUS
        VERSION AND MUST STAY THAT WAY. Every band it names is one DispositionTractionService
        computes - NOT_LISTED, ON_TRACK, CHECKPOINT_DUE at day 30, REVIEW_OVERDUE at day 40,
        HARD_STOP at day 60 ... THE WEEK-NUMBERED MILESTONES OF THE OLD 6-WEEK CLOCK ARE BANNED
        STRINGS in lwc/listingAlerts/__tests__/listingAlerts.test.js".
        WHAT CHANGED: the user settled the third dispute over these thresholds on 2026-08-21 in
        favour of WEEK 1 / WEEK 4 / WEEK 6 (days 7/28/42), overriding DPEG-Stage-by-Stage.docx,
        and added a rule that a logged offer PAUSES the clock at the offer date. The week wording
        is therefore no longer banned in the LWC suite - what that suite still bans, and what this
        text must still never say, is that anyone is EMAILED, ALERTED or FLAGGED.
        🔴 THE PRINCIPLE THAT DID NOT CHANGE, AND IS THE ONLY REASON THIS NOTE EXISTS: every band
        named here is one DispositionTractionService computes, and that service decides a band
        nowhere else. This text must never state a threshold it does not hold. If the ladder moves
        a fourth time, this string moves in the same commit.
        ⚠ "Escalation to Ali" was dropped from this text in 2026-08-10 and must not come back: it
        promised a notification nothing sends - and the 2026-08-21 change explicitly deferred
        emails again.

        THE CLOSING STEP'S THIRD SENTENCE WAS REWRITTEN, AND ITS TWIN ON
        Disposition_Path_Off_Market CARRIES THE IDENTICAL NEW SENTENCE. These two must stay in
        step with each other - they always have. What changed: the old sentence explained that
        the AdminOnly approval lock would silently stop Wire_Verification_Rollup, so the user had
        to remember to verify the wire FIRST. Closing_Approval now carries
        Wire_Verification_Completed__c as an ENTRY CRITERION, so the ordering is enforced rather
        than merely signposted, and the Submit Closing Approval button is hidden until the flag
        is true. The sentence now says what the user will actually experience.

        THE LOI AND PSA STEPS' "arrives in a later change" TEXT IS GONE, BECAUSE IT IS NO LONGER
        TRUE. DispositionStageEntryService auto-creates the sell-side LOI on entry to LOI, and
        Contract_Review__c has a Disposition_PSA record type; both surface in the LOIs and
        Contract Reviews related lists already on Disposition_Record_Page.

        Step ORDER in this file is the design's path order for readability. Runtime display order
        comes from the Disposition_Stage__c picklist value order (sorted = false) filtered by the
        record type, NOT from this file - a retrieve will re-serialise these alphabetically. The
        master value order was deliberately INTERLEAVED (not appended) in the same change so that
        both record types' filtered sequences stay monotonic; the arithmetic is written out in
        objects/Disposition__c/fields/Disposition_Stage__c.field-meta.xml.
    -->
    <active>true</active>
    <entityName>Disposition__c</entityName>
    <fieldName>Disposition_Stage__c</fieldName>
    <masterLabel>Disposition Path On Market</masterLabel>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Property_Asset__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Confirm the asset metrics and Argus signal support the sell decision. Use Submit Sale Decision to send it to the principals; approval moves this deal to BOV Outreach on its own, so there is no Advance button here.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Disposition Readiness</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Package_Sent__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Submission_Deadline__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Send OM packages to 5-6 brokers. The comparison matrix auto-generates when 3+ BOV responses are received. Mark the winning response Selected, then use Submit Selected Broker; approval of that submission moves this deal to Broker Selection.</info>
        <picklistValueName>BOV Outreach</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Selected_Broker__c</fieldNames>
        <info>The approved broker is stamped here from the winning BOV submission. Once the listing agreement is in place, use Advance to NDA. Replacing the broker later requires a fresh approval and does not move the stage back.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Broker Selection</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>NDA_Count__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Signed_NDA_Count__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Send an NDA to each interested party - one NDA record per party, using the NDAs related list below. Nothing is released until every NDA that was not Declined reads Signed; Advance to Release Materials is refused until then.</info>
        <picklistValueName>NDA</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Package_Sent__c</fieldNames>
        <info>The NDAs are signed, so the offering materials can go out. Send the package to the cleared parties, then use Advance to Active Listing to start the marketing clock.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Release Materials</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Selected_Broker__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Listing_Date__c</fieldNames>
        <info>The six-week marketing clock runs from the Listing Date on this Disposition and does not start until that date is set. Traction means logged offers and nothing else. With none: week 1 is a broker check-in, week 4 is At Risk, and week 6 is Hard Stop, where the team decides internally whether to change the broker. A logged offer clears the check-ins at any point and pauses the clock at the offer date.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Active Listing</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Accepted_Offer_Price__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Use Select Offer to pick one of the logged offers. Selecting it moves the deal here and sends that offer to the principals in one step. If they reject it the deal stays on this step so another offer can be selected; approval moves it to LOI.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Offer Selection</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>The sell-side LOI record is created automatically on entry to this step and appears in the LOIs related list below. Negotiate it there, then use Advance to PSA once terms are agreed.</info>
        <picklistValueName>LOI</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <info>The sell-side contract is tracked on a Contract Review record of the Disposition PSA type, in the Contract Reviews related list below. When it reaches Executed, this deal moves to Closing on its own.</info>
        <picklistValueName>PSA</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>PSA_Executed__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Title_Company__c</fieldNames>
        <info>PSA Executed = TRUE spawns closing tasks. Wire fraud prevention gate (6 fields) must be complete before wiring. Complete the wire verification first: the Submit Closing Approval button stays hidden until Wire Verification Completed is true, because the approval both requires it and locks this record while it is pending.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Closing</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <pathAssistantSteps>
        <fieldNames>Closing_Date__c</fieldNames>
        <fieldNames>Net_Sale_Proceeds__c</fieldNames>
        <info>Deal closed. Confirm the closing date, net sale proceeds, and that the closing statement is on file.</info>
        <picklistValueName>Sale Closes</picklistValueName>
    </pathAssistantSteps>
    <recordTypeName>On_Market</recordTypeName>
</PathAssistant>
